# .gitignore for bio-tools
#
# Goal: Prevent committing huge or regenerable content while keeping the
#       repository useful as a collection of scripts + the minimal reference
#       "source" assets needed to reproduce builds.
#
# What we intentionally keep (examples):
#   - All the .sh / .py / .pl scripts
#   - Documentation (READMEs, AGENTS.md, NOTES.md, METHODS.md, etc.)
#   - Minimal "source" reference pieces under mapping/ that are needed to
#     reproduce index builds (the committed GRCh38Patch*.fa.gz, GCA_*.fna.gz,
#     and the additional_*.alt files that have been explicitly added).
#   - Example output PDFs in results/ that serve as qualitative references.
#
# What we do NOT want in the repo:
#   - Massive generated index directories (~100+ GB)
#   - Full source trees of vendored third-party tools (e.g. DeDup/)
#   - Full source + build artifacts of build-time dependencies (util/src/ ~1GB+)
#   - Large downloaded public datasets (YBrowse markers etc. under resources/)
#   - Python/Java build caches, logs, editor droppings, experiment outputs
#   - Any modern/personal sample data (see privacy section below)
#
# Regenerate with:
#   ./util/build_env.sh
#   cd mapping && ./GRCh38_bwa_index.sh
#   ./annotate/fetch_ybrowse_markers.sh
#   ./annotate/prepare_y_refs.sh
#   (and the various liftover / experiment drivers)
#
# For real sample work (especially modern/private), run outside this tree
# and/or use Y_RESOURCES_DIR, BIO_TOOLS_INDEX_DIR, TMP, etc. See AGENTS.md.

# =============================================================================
# Large generated outputs, build trees, and vendored third-party code
# =============================================================================

# BWA / samtools / bcftools / htslib / bedtools / fastp full source + objects
# produced by util/build_env.sh
util/src/

# The actual BWA indices + .dict/.fai etc. (output of GRCh38_bwa_index.sh)
mapping/index/

# DeDup: third-party vendored aDNA deduplication tool (not our code).
# Entire tree ignored (it carries its own .git, LICENSE, full source, Gradle build).
# We only reference it locally for aDNA workflows.
DeDup/

# =============================================================================
# Python
# =============================================================================
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# =============================================================================
# Fetched / downloaded large public data (regenerable via scripts)
# =============================================================================
#
# annotate/ Y-chromosome workflows fetch YBrowse markers and GFF3 here,
# plus liftover chains and staged references. These files are large and
# can be re-fetched. Use Y_RESOURCES_DIR to redirect outside the repo if
# you prefer to keep a local mirror.

resources/

# Legacy / alternate location some older scripts or fallbacks use
annotate/data/

# Catch marker files if a fetch or copy lands them directly in annotate/
annotate/snps_hg38.vcf.gz
annotate/snps_hg38.vcf.gz.tbi
annotate/snps_hg38.gff3

# =============================================================================
# Logs, temporary, and backup files
# =============================================================================
*.log
util/build.log
**/*~
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
**/*.swp
**/*.swo

# =============================================================================
# Editor, IDE, and operating system cruft
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-*

# =============================================================================
# Other common build / stray artifacts (most are already covered by the
# directory rules above)
# =============================================================================
**/.gradle/

# =============================================================================
# AI coding assistant local state (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.)
# Keep the committed instruction files (AGENTS.md, mapping/CLAUDE.md) but
# ignore per-user / per-session settings and caches.
# =============================================================================
**/.claude/
**/.cursor/
**/.windsurf/

# Local tool setups (Codex exporter skills, etc.)
.agents/
.clawhub/

# =============================================================================
# Local experiment / analysis output directories
# The Y-liftover and modern sample experiment drivers document that you
# should run them from a private directory outside this repo. Ignore the
# conventional names in case someone runs them here by accident.
# =============================================================================
experiments/
local-analysis/
private/

# Exported chat logs from other tools (Codex, etc.) — often contain private paths/data
codex-session.md
*-session.md
codex-*.md
*.codex*

# =============================================================================
# Personal / modern sample data guardrails
# See "Data Handling & Privacy" and Y/Liftover Guardrails in AGENTS.md
#
# Core rule: Modern/private human datasets must never enter git history.
#   - No sample identifiers, read names, or raw data.
#   - No VCF/gVCF contents or derived per-sample reports from living or
#     modern individuals.
#   - Ancient/public datasets (e.g. published Iceman/Otzi) are explicitly
#     allowed and may be committed with proper documentation.
#
# Practical defense layers:
#   - Scripts instruct you to run sensitive work from an external
#     <private_analysis_dir>.
#   - Use placeholders (<sample_id>, etc.) in any committed notes.
#   - This .gitignore provides a safety net against accidental inclusion.
#
# If you ever need to force something (public example data only), use
# `git add -f`, but prefer to keep even examples minimal.
# =============================================================================

# Per-sample or private genomic data formats.
# (Public YBrowse marker sets are fetched into resources/ and annotate/data/,
#  which are already fully ignored above. Reference genomes use .fa.gz/.fna.gz.)
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.gvcf
*.gvcf.gz
*.bcf

# Alignment files from personal sequencing runs
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.crai

# Fastq / raw reads (should never be here anyway)
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq
*.fq.gz

# Common patterns for personal analysis outputs
*personal*
*private*
modern*.tsv
sample_*.tsv
*_realigned.*
*_deduped.*


# Third-party genealogy/project pages (FTDNA, YFull, etc.) — contain kit numbers,
# surnames and paternal-ancestor details of living people. Keep in <private_refs_dir>.
*.html
*.htm
FamilyTreeDNA*
YFull*
